.TH MYPROX2 1 "2026-10-12" "prox2 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
myprox2 \- GNOME app for the Logitech PRO X Superlight 2 mouse
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B myprox2
.RB [ \-\-background ]
.RB [ \-\-falso ]
.RB [ \-\-simular\-bateria
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-simular\-carga ]
.br
.B myprox2
.RB { instalar\-local | desinstalar\-local }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B myprox2
is a native GNOME app (GTK 4 and libadwaita) built on the same code as
.BR prox2 (1).
It shows the mouse battery, with an icon in the top bar (tray) and notifications,
and has a window with the profile slots and DPI, a "Botões" tab
(5 buttons on 2 layers, normal and G\-Shift) and a "Macros" tab.
The menu has "Iniciar com a sessão" to start the app with the session.
For the tray icon on GNOME, install gnome\-shell\-extension\-appindicator.
.SH OPTIONS
Without options the window opens.
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start without a window, only the tray icon.
.TP
.B \-\-falso
Use a simulated mouse in memory. It does not touch the real mouse,
so it is safe for trying the interface.
The battery level is 80 unless \-\-simular\-bateria is given.
.TP
.BI \-\-simular\-bateria " N"
Simulate battery level N.
.TP
.B \-\-simular\-carga
Simulate a charging battery. Without \-\-simular\-bateria, the level is 50.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B instalar\-local
Add the app to the menu for the current user (.desktop file and icon), pointing at the
current copy of the code. It refuses to run when the app came from the package.
.TP
.B desinstalar\-local
Remove the files written by
.BR instalar\-local .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/myproX2/
Backup and data. Follows XDG_DATA_HOME.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/io.github.jonanthann.myproX2.desktop
Created by "Iniciar com a sessão"; starts the app with
.BR \-\-background .
Follows XDG_CONFIG_HOME.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications/io.github.jonanthann.myproX2.desktop
Menu entry written by
.BR instalar\-local .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/io.github.jonanthann.myproX2.svg
Icon written by
.BR instalar\-local .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60\-prox2.rules
Gives the logged in user access to the receiver hidraw device.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
myprox2
myprox2 \-\-background
myprox2 \-\-falso
myprox2 \-\-simular\-bateria 15
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR prox2 (1)
.SH AUTHOR
jonanthann
